      "date": "2026-11-02 19:02:38.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(7 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nMostly good. The ZFS path is unchanged and the LVM path behaves as before. I found no defects, only the minor comments inline, so there is no need to re-spin for them alone.\n\nThe md backend itself has no test results. CI has no md-kmec arrays, and the commit message doesn't say whether sanity-lsnapshot was run against one by hand. Could the results of such a run be added? A pointer to where `mdadm --snapshot` is documented (which mdadm/md-kmec version) would also help: the --create/--attr/--tag/--set/--rename/--exists/--list --export syntax and the one-line, space-separated `--export` output that lvm_read_tags() and snapshot_list_all() parse can't be checked against anything in this tree.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    },
