          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Hiroshi Nishida",
          "email": "hnishida@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-31 05:10:28.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Hiroshi Nishida",
          "email": "hnishida@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-02 22:16:50.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21089 utils: add md-kmec native backend to lctl snapshot",
        "message": "LU-21089 utils: add md-kmec native backend to lctl snapshot\n\nlctl snapshot_* works for ZFS targets and for ldiskfs on LVM thin\nLVs. Native snapshots are a new md-kmec feature: crash-safe,\nread-only snapshots of a whole raidkm array, managed with\n\"mdadm --snapshot\".\n\nAccept \"md:/dev/<array>\" devices in ldev.conf. The snapshot piece\nis the native snapshot <ssname> of the array, made with\n\"mdadm --snapshot <array> --create\", which freezes the filesystem\non the array itself. Its read-only device comes from --list, and\nthe lustre_* attributes are the same as the LVM tags. Pieces are\nmounted with rdonly_dev and fsname=, as for LVM. snapshot_create\nfirst checks that each md: array supports native snapshots.\n\nLet sanity-lsnapshot detect md: targets, and document md: for\nlctl snapshot in lctl.8 and ldev.conf.5. CI has no md-kmec arrays,\nso CI only checks that the ZFS path is unchanged.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial fstype=zfs testlist=sanity-lsnapshot\nSigned-off-by: Hiroshi Nishida <hnishida@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: Id00e4143c6fe24042f186c3ad4f61089c4ca6202\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
